### What steps can reproduce the bug?

With hono/jsx/dom, useEffect cleanup does not run when tearing down via `render(null, container)`. `createRoot().unmount()` does run cleanup.

Minimal reproduction:

```ts
import { useEffect } from "hono/jsx";
import { render } from "hono/jsx/dom";

function Portal() {
  useEffect(() => {
    const el = document.createElement("div");
    el.setAttribute("data-portal", "");
    el.textContent = "hello";
    document.body.appendChild(el);
    return () => el.remove();
  }, []);
  return <div aria-hidden style={{ visibility: "hidden" }}>hello</div>;
}

const container = document.createElement("div");
document.body.appendChild(container);

render(<Portal />, container);
// document.querySelector("[data-portal]") exists

render(null, container);
// [data-portal] is STILL present (cleanup did not run)

// Workaround:
// const root = createRoot(container);
// root.render(<Portal />);
// root.unmount(); // cleanup runs
```

### What is the expected behavior?

Aligned with React’s client APIs:

1. root.render accepts null as a valid React node
   (https://react.dev/reference/react-dom/client/createRoot#root-render):
   “you can also pass … null, or undefined.”

2. Unmount tears down the tree and cleans up resources
   (https://react.dev/reference/react-dom/client/createRoot#root-unmount):
   “Calling root.unmount will unmount all the components in the root and
   detach React from the root DOM node, including removing any event
   handlers or state in the tree.”

3. useEffect cleanup runs when a component unmounts
   (https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect).

So either `render(null, container)` should cause effect cleanups to run,
or the docs should state that only `createRoot().unmount()` guarantees
teardown.

### What do you see instead?

`render(null, container)` does not run useEffect cleanup.
Nodes appended to document.body in the effect remain.

`createRoot(container).render(...)` followed by `root.unmount()` does run
cleanup and removes the portal.

